Java Study Companion

A simple, student-focused Android app for learning Java and Object-Oriented Programming

Course: UGICT22J301 – Understanding OOPs through Java
Platform: Android
Project type: Educational application
Developer: Haris Shameem
Repository: "Java Study Companion on GitHub" (https://github.com/harryisfedup2/UGICT22J301_StudyCompanion)

---

About the Project

Java Study Companion is an Android learning application developed to make studying Java and Object-Oriented Programming more accessible, organised and convenient for students.

The aim of this project is to bring important theory concepts and practical Java programs together in one place, with a clean, minimal and student-friendly interface.

The application is designed as a study companion for students following the UGICT22J301 – Understanding OOPs through Java course.

Key Features

- Four Theory Units: Organised learning material covering the four units of the course.
- 30 Java Practical Programs: A dedicated practical section containing 30 Java programs.
- Concept-Based Learning: Explanations and definitions to support understanding of important topics and subtopics.
- Code and Expected Output: Practical examples presented with their Java source code and expected output.
- Minimalist Interface: A clean, focused design intended to make reading and navigation comfortable.
- Student-Friendly Access: Study material and practical examples available directly on an Android device.

