Download and Installation

Option 1 – Download the Android App

Download the APK from the repository's Releases section:

"Java Study Companion – Releases" (https://github.com/harryisfedup2/UGICT22J301_StudyCompanion/releases)

1. Download the latest APK.
2. Open the downloaded APK on your Android device.
3. If Android asks for permission, allow installation from that source.
4. Complete the installation and open Java Study Companion.

Option 2 – Download the Source Code

Visit the repository:

"View Java Study Companion Source Code" (https://github.com/harryisfedup2/UGICT22J301_StudyCompanion)

Select Code → Download ZIP to download the project.

You can open the extracted project in Android Studio to explore the code, learn how the application is structured, make modifications and build your own version.

